. /****************************************************************************
> ***
>  TAB_01.do -- TAB step: table cells with no corrected-vintage estimate yet (o
> ne vintage per run).
>  Usage (cwd = 02_code/10_analysis):  "$STATA" -b -q do TAB_01.do <vintage>   
>   (vintage = submitted | corrected)
>  Specification = File S1 code (run_tests.do T5/T10/T11/T12, run_T6.do) and PK
> G 03_table1_descriptives.do:
>    ppmlhdfe y x [if], absorb(exporter_year importer_year pair_id) vce(cluster
>  pair_id); same FE/cluster as the paper.
>  Items (all on out/<vintage>/prepared.dta; no data value is altered, restrict
> ions are if-conditions):
>    T1.*   Table 1 descriptive statistics (summarize on the full prepared file
> )
>    T11.*  Table 7 Panel B: exclude pair-years above the 99.9th percentile of 
> each directional flow
>           (run_tests.do:289-309; reverse and same-direction cutoffs separatel
> y for "directional")
>    T10.*  Table 7 Panel C: same_basis==1 (stored direction) and same_basis in
>  both directions
>           (run_tests.do:264-275; same_basis, cd6_strict from the vintage's ow
> n master, as construct_metadata.do)
>    T6.*   Table A5 artworks HS 9701-9703 (v_art3) and publications excl. 4907
> /4908/4911 (v_pub_core)
>           (run_T6.do:42-61; PREP rebuilt the HS6 outcomes from the raw API fi
> les)
>    T12.*  Table A5 visitor-minus-tourist difference, alone and controlling fo
> r tourists (run_tests.do:312-324)
>    T5.*   Table A5 cultural distance requiring all six Hofstede dimensions (r
> un_tests.do:176-206, strict part)
>  Help files consulted (installed): ppmlhdfe.sthlp 2.3.4 (e(converged) l.287, 
> e(N_full) l.261,
>  e(num_singletons) l.259, e(num_separated) l.260; absorb(), vce(cluster)), [R
> ] lincom (level(), r(estimate)
>  r(se) r(p) r(lb) r(ub), lincom.sthlp l.191-196), [R] pctile/_pctile (percent
> ile in r(r1), pctile.sthlp l.195),
>  [R] summarize (r(N) r(mean) r(sd) r(min) r(max)), [D] merge (1:1, keep(), as
> sert), nflow.sthlp (start/step/est).
>  Every ppmlhdfe fit: assert e(converged)==1 and e(N_full)==e(N)+e(num_singlet
> ons)+e(num_separated).
> *****************************************************************************
> **/
. args vintage

. clear all

. set more off

. set varabbrev off

. set linesize 200

. version 18.0

. do "00_config.do" `vintage'

. /*******************************************************************************
>  00_config.do  --  globals for one data vintage (analysis layer of the replication package)
> 
>  Usage (from another do-file, cwd = 02_code/10_analysis):  do 00_config.do <vintage>
>    <vintage> = corrected2x (revised baseline, default run)
>              | corrected | corrected2 (reconciliation switch, same data build)
>              | submitted (reconciliation switch, needs a second build with corrections off)
>  Every path is built from the package root ${PKGROOT}, which run_all.py passes as the first
>  argument of the generated wrapper do-file (_run.do pattern); nothing here is machine-specific.
>  Defines globals only and checks the Stata version.
> 
>  Vintages (see README.md, "Data-correction rules"):
>    corrected   = build with the correction rules on (code 490 -> TWN, Paraguay residence quarantine, flags)
>    corrected2  = corrected + quarantine of PAK residence 2020-2021 and BLR visitors-by-residence
>                  partner LIE 2020-2022 (same rule as Paraguay); 31-code outcome
>    corrected2x = corrected2 with the 30-code outcome (31-code basket minus HS 490700) = revised baseline
>    submitted   = original data as submitted (build with corrections off), for the reconciliation only
> *******************************************************************************/
. 
